course: dictionary
lesson: 15091
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word roots is one of them. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it. «The roots of the oak tree spread far under the lawn» tells you the roots are under the ground, because they spread under the lawn.
explain: Now read this: «Maria has Italian roots, and her family still cooks pasta on Sundays.» Roots here does not mean plant parts. It means where a family comes from. The words family and Italian are the clues.
explain: Try the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence in place of the word. «Maria has Italian origins» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Always check that your meaning fits the whole sentence, not just one part.
explain: In maths, «The square root of 25 is 5» uses the same word for a different idea. A root is a number that multiplies by itself to give another number: 5 × 5 = 25. The context is maths, so the meaning is clear.
fact: Roots are the parts of a plant that grow under the ground. They hold the plant in place and take in water.
fact: The roots of a tooth or a hair are the parts that hold it in the body.
fact: «Roots» can also mean where you come from, or where a problem starts.
fact: The square root of 9 is 3, because 3 × 3 = 9.
fact: A root word is the main part of a word before prefixes and suffixes are added. Happy is the root word of unhappiness.
exercise: «The oak tree's roots spread under the lawn.» What are roots in this sentence? | *The parts of a plant under the ground that hold it in place | The birds nesting in the crown | The branches that reach up to the sky | The leaves at the top of the tree
exercise: «Her grandmother's roots are in Greece, so the family often cooks Greek food.» What does roots mean here? | A sharp pain in the back | A kind of tree that grows in Greece | The parts of a plant under the soil | *Where her family comes from
exercise: «The square root of 16 is 4, because 4 × 4 = 16.» In maths, what is a root? | A number that is always bigger than the answer | A shape with four equal sides | *A number that multiplies by itself to give another number | A sum of two numbers added together
test: «The dentist could see the roots of the tooth on the X-ray.» What are the roots of a tooth? | *The parts that hold it in the jaw | The sweets that the tooth likes | The white top part you can see | The sugar that the tooth eats
test: «Sam wanted to find the roots of the argument so it would not happen again.» What does roots mean here? | *The place where the argument started | The trees near the school | The loud voices in the argument | The people who watched it
exam: «Which number is the square root of 25?» | *5 | 625 | 12 | 2
